<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36635" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξᾰλᾰπ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sack, storm,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.40
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				1.129
			</span></i>, etc.; also, <i>empty</i> a city <i>of its inhabitants,
				clear</i> it <i>out,</i> so as to plant new settlers in it, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίαν πόλιν ἐξαλαπάξας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.176
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>destroy utterly,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆας, τεῖχος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.813
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				20.30
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλά με νόσος ἐξαλάπαξεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					2.85
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			 word, used by <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.1.29
			</span></i>.</div>
